  "body": "## Context\n\n`STATUS.md` is the ledger of which `SPEC.md` requirements the code meets, and it was overstating: a full audit found 209 of 280 Covered where it claimed 259, with seven requirements whose text contradicted the code. This trues the ledger up and works toward full reconciliation: the contradictions are settled, the commit flow now commits exactly what was reviewed, and helpers that gave a confident wrong answer report what's actually true. The ledger ends at 231 Covered, 38 Partial, 11 Missing, none contradicting.\n\nCloses #98\nCloses #116\nRefs #79, #46\n\n## Review guide\n\n**Pipeline reads and the merge gate** (highest stakes: these decide whether a merge goes through)\n- [`scripts/pipeline-status.sh`](https://github.com/chris-peterson/anchor/pull/143/changes#diff-3045d80a02002fe4cea8c8556c336ffcd0666c12001b07918d0b0e91b783d26bR80): a forge read that fails is `unreachable` with the CLI's error, not `none`, and ends a watch at once\n- [`scripts/merge-gates.sh`](https://github.com/chris-peterson/anchor/pull/143/changes#diff-adeebce24896e76808a2e1ef646a547027a304247f454b43270e9de3079d1b22R269): a GitHub `BLOCKED` PR with a failing check blocks at the pipeline gate; `skipped` passes like `none`; `unreachable` blocks\n\n**Commit what was reviewed**\n- [`scripts/review-diff.sh`](https://github.com/chris-peterson/anchor/pull/143/changes#diff-316ff65ec872e9469328f85bc6cc55c751739cd343ba7900bc969a4120920cefR482): the `--local` review shows the named paths only, in revdiff, a difftool, and the edit buffer\n- [`scripts/lib/stage-paths.sh`](https://github.com/chris-peterson/anchor/pull/143/changes#diff-658642383ab52bb544fd95b21498feef9778472c5a185e49cea9977cacb59562R113): a named rename carries its old name into the review, the review id, and the commit\n- [`scripts/commit.sh`](https://github.com/chris-peterson/anchor/pull/143/changes#diff-1bc6837e9fe0d02660b6de15bb18e07ac27802323ccdbf9b280d14197e8cd064R196): a commit a hook changed stays local (exit 71); an amend re-reads the squash gate (exit 69) and a message-only amend uses `--only`\n\n**Smaller wrong answers**\n- [`scripts/release-recon.sh`](https://github.com/chris-peterson/anchor/pull/143/changes#diff-71d68889414ad7fb53481c30eb61790780dd1e6a1916b9962078de050ea50297R200): one-line `on:` triggers, and a `version` input that takes an exact version\n- [`scripts/review-post.sh`](https://github.com/chris-peterson/anchor/pull/143/changes#diff-0fce35f41cdd1f6de69797305d3a6b2a9fabcbabd1b0f01b1375eac187c8831fR86): a line outside every hunk folds into the summary; a failure partway reports what posted\n- [`scripts/review/modes/diff.sh`](https://github.com/chris-peterson/anchor/pull/143/changes#diff-8f62fb2e9f4fc7e854c0f247c202dc40750506ba95b3e872006795b1a7b0801fR110) and [`scripts/lib/review-editor.sh`](https://github.com/chris-peterson/anchor/pull/143/changes#diff-da97bdf97af2c8cfbe46289d2c0259b90314b6f8edcc6ceb45e732bf3e267be5R55): a difftool review of a commit range is `no-verdict`; an unset `GIT_EDITOR` no longer reads as git's `vi`\n\n**Spec and ledger**\n- `SPEC.md`: five requirements reworded to what the code does, COMMIT-17 and PREPARE-10b retired, COMMIT-04b/04d/04e and the bug fixes' requirements amended\n- [`STATUS.md`](https://github.com/chris-peterson/anchor/pull/143/changes#diff-6c33a39439907887e8de50ebb50d264136cb2a7c916dc8d4c184ee24fb5cec9eR8): per-category gaps and the decisions still open\n\nPath scoping was checked in live reviews with revdiff, hx, and kdiff3, and `unreachable` against GitHub with a bad token.\n",
